# P_common package set - the single source of truth for the cloud-provision
# operator definition. docs/IMAGE_WORKFLOW.md (Operator definition, P_common)
# describes the structure and references this file; the package-parity guard in
# tests/check-package-parity.bash derives each OS's expected list from it.
# Package names live only here.
#
# Format: one "key: values" line per group. Blank lines and # comments ignored.
# The guard enforces this source's integrity and otherwise fails loudly:
#   - keys are limited to must_have, core, debian_only, spelling, and family;
#   - each key appears on exactly one line;
#   - family values are debian or rocky only (ubuntu spells like debian).
# The single source is cloud-provision-local; the ansible-provision common role
# keeps its own installer list, which this guard does not compare against (D020).

must_have: sudo chrony git wget unzip gcc g++ make autoconf automake libtool ssl-dev net-tools
core: vim tmux lsof tree sysstat logrotate acl socat
debian_only: locales

# canonical-name=debian-spelling:rocky-spelling, only where the two families differ
spelling: ssl-dev=libssl-dev:openssl-devel g++=g++:gcc-c++

# base OS type -> package family (the debian family covers debian and ubuntu)
family: debian12=debian debian13=debian ubuntu24=debian ubuntu26=debian rocky8=rocky rocky10=rocky
